    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d499">

                <pb facs="0557" n="507" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg507"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. McDonald to Mr.
                            Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Teheran</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-01-22"><hi rendition="#italic">January 22, 1894</hi></date>.
                        (Received March 5.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 62.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to forward, herewith
                    inclosed, a copy of a letter I have received from Dr. J. P. Cochran, of
                    Oroomiah. * * *</p>
                <p>It is satisfactory to observe from Dr. Cochran’s letter that during the time of
                    great anxiety following the murder of Aga Jan, and on the occasion of the
                    outrage on Mr. St. Pierre, the missionaries have acted with most commendable
                    self-control and circumspection, and in their communications with the Government
                    authorities relative to these crimes they have been very careful and
                    discreet.</p>
                <p>I also inclose my reply to Dr. Cochran’s letter.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alex. McDonald.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d499-a1.xml" xpointer="d499-a1"/>
